'''''Polypogon viridis''''', the '''beardless rabbitsfoot grass''', '''water bent''', is a species of perennial grass in the family [[Poaceae]] (true grasses). They have a self-supporting growth form and simple, broad leaves. Individuals can grow to 0.43 m.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Polypogon viridis (Gouan) Breistr. - Encyclopedia of Life|url=https://eol.org/pages/1115515|access-date=2022-02-04|website=eol.org}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mifsud |first=Stephen |date=2002-08-23 |title=Polypogon viridis (Water Bent Grass) : MaltaWildPlants.com - the online Flora of the Maltese Islands. |url=https://www.maltawildplants.com/POAC/Polypogon_viridis.php |access-date=2022-03-07 |website=www.maltawildplants.com |language=en-us}}</ref> They are native to southern Europe, [[Macaronesia]], North and East Africa, western and central Asia, India, Yunnan, and Vietnam.<ref>{{cite web |title=''Polypogon viridis'' (Gouan) Breistr. {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:418741-1 |website=Plants of the World Online |access-date=1 September 2023 |language=en}}</ref> 

It is a common established neophyte in the UK.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Stroh |first1=P. A. |last2=Walker |first2=K. J. |last3=Humphrey |first3=T. A. |last4=Burkmar |first4=R. J. |last5=Pescott |first5=O. L. |last6=Roy |first6=D. B. |title=''Polypogon viridis'' (Gouan) Breistr. |url=https://plantatlas2020.org/atlas/2cd4p9h.eee |website=Plant Atlas 2020 |publisher=Botanical Society of Britain and Ireland |access-date=22 December 2025 |year=2023}}</ref>

